    {
      "sort_order": 1,
      "title_en": "Opposites at the Zoo",
      "body_en": "On Saturday, Mom took Nong Fah, Thawan, and Bua to the zoo.\n\nFirst they saw a big elephant. Next to it was a small mouse.\n\nA tall giraffe stretched its long neck up high. A short cat sat on a rock.\n\nThe rabbits ran fast. The turtle walked slowly.\n\nIn the reptile house, the lizards liked it hot. The penguins swam in cold water.\n\nBua's shirt was clean, but after she chased a duck near a puddle, her shorts were dirty.\n\nThey bought popcorn. The bag was full. After everyone shared, the bag was empty.\n\n\"So many opposites today!\" said Bua."
    },
    {
      "sort_order": 2,
      "title_en": "A Wonderful Day",
      "body_en": "Nong Fah woke up. Her pillow was soft and her blanket was warm.\n\nIn the kitchen she ate a sweet cupcake. Then she tasted a lemon. It was very sour!\n\nAt school her teacher gave the children round oranges and flat pancakes.\n\nThawan showed her a rough brown rock and a smooth blue marble.\n\nAt recess a small boy fell off the swing. Nong Fah helped him up. \"You are very kind,\" said his mother.\n\nIn class the maths problems were hard, but Ollie helped them. \"You are so smart!\" said Thawan.\n\nThat night Nong Fah went to bed under her soft blanket. It had been a wonderful day."
    },
    {
      "sort_order": 3,
      "title_en": "My Family Tree",
      "body_en": "My name is Nong Fah. Let me tell you about my family.\n\nMy parents are my mother and my father. My mother is kind and gentle. My father works in an office.\n\nMy mother's parents are my grandmother and my grandfather. They live near us. My grandmother bakes sweet cookies. My grandfather tells stories about when he was a boy.\n\nI have one big brother and one little sister. We share our toys.\n\nMy mother has a sister. She is my aunt. Her son is my cousin. We are the same age!\n\nEvery Sunday the whole family eats lunch together at one big table."
    }
  ],
